su - become another user

SYNOPSIS
    su [USER]

DESCRIPTION
    Starts a shell as USER, or as root if none is named. Asks for that user's
    password unless the caller is already root.

    Authentication goes to authd, which is a separate process: the password
    file is not readable by whoever is asking, and this program never sees
    the hash.

SEE ALSO
    id, whoami, login
